EOF Analysis on SST Datasets — Observation, Free, and Assimilation Experiments
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repository contains a series of Jupyter notebooks performing Empirical Orthogonal Function (EOF) analyses on Sea Surface Temperature (SST) fields from various datasets and ocean model experiments.
The objective is to compare the dominant variability patterns of SST under different configurations — from pure observations to several assimilation schemes.
Datasets and Experiments
------------------------
Hadley Observation — SST observational dataset used as reference.
Free Run (No Assimilation) — model simulation without any data assimilation.
ODA (Oceanic Data Assimilation) — simulation with SST assimilation using the Deekman Filter method.
NudF-UVT & NudA-UVT — experiments with assimilation of U, V, and T parameters through Newtonian relaxation (nudging), applied respectively to full-field and anomaly states.
NudA-UV — assimilation of U and V components only, using the same nudging approach.
Purpose
-------
The EOF analysis is used to:
Identify the main spatial and temporal modes of SST variability.
Compare how different assimilation methods affect the representation of dominant SST patterns.
Quantify the variance explained by each mode across experiments.
